# 10. AUTOMATIC NEXT-LESSON PROMPT ASSEMBLY

## 10.1. Main objective

Once a valid report has been saved, the platform must automatically prepare the next lesson prompt.

No generative AI is used.

The composition must be deterministic.

## 10.2. Carryover engine

Develop a `PromptAssemblyService`.

Responsibilities:

- Retrieve the published prompt for the next lesson.
- Retrieve the prior lesson result.
- Retrieve mandatory rechecks.
- Retrieve outstanding homework.
- Retrieve persistent older gaps.
- Retrieve relevant mentor instructions.
- Assemble and format the final prompt.
- Prevent duplicate instructions.
- Preserve every mandatory error recheck.
- Save the generated prompt snapshot.

## 10.3. Prompt composition behavior

The next prompt should start with a structured carryover section.

Example:

**«ВХОДНЫЕ ИНСТРУКЦИИ ДЛЯ M01-T01-U02»**

Include:

- What was studied.
- Previous assessment results.
- Every error requiring rechecking.
- Homework to be verified.
- Other important previous-lesson knowledge.
- Persistent gaps.
- Explicit instructions prohibiting hints during entry testing.

Then insert the official content of the next lesson according to the configured assembly format.

## 10.4. No loss of errors

If the previous lesson contains three mandatory rechecks, the next lesson must include all three.

If an error persists across multiple lessons, retain it in the knowledge gap registry until resolved according to the course rules.

## 10.5. Idempotency

Submitting the same report twice must not duplicate:

- Progress.
- Skills.
- Mandatory rechecks.
- Homework.
- Administrator notifications.

Store unique attempt IDs and report IDs.

