# 15. ASSESSMENTS, CONTROL WORKS AND EXAMS

## 15.1. Assessment hierarchy

Support:

1. Daily lesson assessment.
2. Topic-level control work.
3. Discipline final exam.
4. Retake attempts.

These must be distinct assessment types.

## 15.2. Control works

Administrators can create and publish control works associated with completed topics.

Store:

- Title.
- Covered topics.
- Questions.
- Practical tasks.
- Maximum points.
- Passing rules.
- Attempts.
- Student submissions.
- Scores.
- Feedback.

Every control-work result, successful or unsuccessful, must create an administrator notification.

## 15.3. Discipline exam

Each of the 18 disciplines has its own exam.

Plan for approximately 24 tickets per discipline.

Each ticket contains:

- Two theoretical questions.
- One practical assignment.

Question bank constraints per discipline:

- Maximum 50 unique theoretical questions.
- Maximum 25 unique practical assignments.

## 15.4. Open exam bank

**All approved tickets and their complete questions must be openly visible to the student before the exam.**

The exam bank is official preparation material.

Create an exam preparation screen with:

- Full ticket list.
- Theory question catalog.
- Practical assignment catalog.
- Topic filters.
- Links to relevant lessons.
- Preparation status.
- Personal preparation notes.

Do not hide exam questions from the student.

## 15.5. Grading scale

Implement:

- Below 50% — Не зачтено.
- 50% to below 70% — Зачтено.
- 70% to below 80% — Хорошо.
- 80% to 100% — Отлично.

The exact threshold values must be inclusive at 50, 70 and 80.

Use stored scoring rubrics.

Do not allow client-side score manipulation.

## 15.6. Exam score weights

Support administrator-configurable weights.

Suggested default:

- Theory question 1: 30 points.
- Theory question 2: 30 points.
- Practical task: 40 points.

This is a configurable suggestion, not a hardcoded curriculum requirement.

## 15.7. Retakes

If score is below 50%, mark the assessment as not passed.

Permit up to three retakes after the initial attempt, according to administrator-approved policy.

Each attempt is stored separately.

Provide a clear explanation of failed criteria before another attempt.

Notify the administrator when the third retake becomes necessary.

After three unsuccessful retakes, prevent additional attempts until an administrator decides on the next action.

## 15.8. Results from ChatGPT

The platform may import external exam reports.

Imported grades remain student-submitted until reviewed according to administrative policy.

For official confirmed examinations, the administrator must be able to validate the score or administer an independent assessment.

