# 20. PROGRESS COMPUTATION RULES

All progress must be computed from actual stored states.

## 20.1. Lesson completion

A lesson is not completed merely because the prompt was copied.

Completion requires a submitted valid lesson result and fulfillment of the configured progression policy.

## 20.2. Provisional and confirmed status

Maintain separate values:

- Submitted progress.
- Mentor-confirmed progress.

Do not combine the two into one misleading score.

## 20.3. Module completion

Define module completion from:

- Required published lessons.
- Required homework.
- Required control works.
- Final exam status.
- Administrator-configured requirements.

## 20.4. Skill mastery

Use evidence-based status calculation.

Skill completion must not be inferred merely from the existence of a topic title or opening the lesson page.

## 20.5. Configuration

Allow administrators to specify whether:

- A valid student report unlocks the next lesson provisionally.
- Mentor approval is required before unlock.
- Critical gaps block progression.
- Homework completion is required.
- Failed exams block the next module.

For the initial release, allow lesson progression after a structurally valid report submission unless a restriction or critical-gap policy applies, while keeping the result visibly unconfirmed.

Official exam approval must follow the configured verification policy.

