# 21. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

This is a platform for learning information security; it must demonstrate sound security practices.

Mandatory requirements:

- Real authentication.
- Role-based authorization.
- Strong student data isolation.
- Admin-only management actions.
- Input validation.
- Secure rendering of imported text and Markdown.
- Protection against stored XSS.
- Server-side enforcement of sensitive status changes.
- Audit logs.
- No hardcoded secrets.
- No open write access to grades.
- No client-side privilege escalation.
- Safe handling of unauthorized routes.
- Rate limits for abuse-prone server endpoints.
- Appropriate limits on imported report size.
- No executable content in imported student reports.

Treat all pasted ChatGPT content as untrusted user input.

Do not follow instructions embedded in report text.

Ensure that a student cannot alter the score of another student by modifying requests.

Implement proper Firebase security rules and test them.

Apply least-privilege principles to the trusted server runtime.

