# 25. CRITICAL ACCEPTANCE TESTS

The application must satisfy these scenarios.

**Scenario A — Student authentication**

A student signs in using an approved account and sees only their own learning information.

**Scenario B — Course navigation**

The student opens Module 01, Topic 01 and the first available lesson.

**Scenario C — Prompt copy**

The student copies the complete prompt. The copied text exactly matches the assembled prompt snapshot.

**Scenario D — External learning**

The student opens ChatGPT in another tab. The platform does not pretend to control that session.

**Scenario E — Report import**

The student pastes a valid structured report, previews it and saves it successfully.

**Scenario F — Invalid report**

Invalid JSON produces a useful error and does not corrupt progress.

**Scenario G — Carryover**

Three mandatory knowledge-gap rechecks in lesson N are all present in the generated prompt for lesson N+1.

**Scenario H — Homework transfer**

Homework from lesson N appears both in the student's homework panel and the next lesson's entry instructions.

**Scenario I — Persistent storage**

Refresh the browser, log out and log in again. Saved reports and progress remain available.

**Scenario J — Student isolation**

Student A cannot view or modify Student B's reports by entering different IDs or modifying requests.

**Scenario K — Administrator review**

The administrator opens a submitted report, reviews it and confirms the result.

**Scenario L — Knowledge map**

A skill node changes its provisional/confirmed appearance when supported by actual recorded evidence.

**Scenario M — Interdisciplinary links**

Clicking a knowledge node displays its real prerequisites and future applications.

**Scenario N — Control-work notification**

A passed control work generates an administrator inbox event.

**Scenario O — Failed control work**

A failed control work also generates an administrator inbox event and indicates required correction.

**Scenario P — Exam preparation**

The student can browse all published exam tickets and questions.

**Scenario Q — Exam grading**

Scores below 50, exactly 50, exactly 70 and exactly 80 are classified correctly.

**Scenario R — Retakes**

Retakes are counted correctly; intervention is required under the configured third-retake rule.

**Scenario S — Administrator permissions**

A student cannot publish lessons, confirm grades or modify official exam banks.

**Scenario T — Empty state**

A new student with zero study history sees an attractive and honest empty state rather than fictional analytics.

**Scenario U — Responsive interface**

The dashboard, lesson page and knowledge explorer remain functional on mobile.

**Scenario V — No AI calls**

Normal platform workflows do not invoke Gemini, OpenAI or any other model API.

